menu "WiSense Transmitter Configuration"

    config TX_BEACON_PACKET_RATE
        int "Transmission rate (packets/second)"
        default 100
        range 1 500
        help
            Target rate of WiFi broadcast frames transmitted per second (Hz).
            Default is 100 packets/sec (10 ms period), matching the esp-csi
            spike baseline. This rate provides sufficient temporal resolution
            for human micro-Doppler motion sensing while remaining well within
            ESP-NOW's throughput limits. Configurable via menuconfig to support
            empirical rate comparison experiments (e.g., 50 pps vs. 100 pps).

    config TX_BEACON_WIFI_CHANNEL
        int "WiFi Channel (1-13)"
        default 11
        range 1 13
        help
            2.4 GHz WiFi primary channel for packet transmission. Channel 11 is
            selected by default as a standard non-overlapping channel with low
            ambient co-channel interference in our laboratory baseline, and
            matches the channel used during the initial hardware spikes.

    config TX_BEACON_LOG_INTERVAL_SEC
        int "Serial status log interval (seconds)"
        default 1
        range 1 60
        help
            Frequency in seconds at which transmission health statistics
            ([TX_STAT] total count, period packets, device uptime, achieved pps,
            and free heap) are output to the serial monitor.

    config TX_BEACON_PAYLOAD_SIZE
        int "Payload size (bytes)"
        default 32
        range 4 250
        help
            Size in bytes of the ESP-NOW payload. The first 4 bytes contain the
            32-bit packet sequence number (matching rx_id in csi_recv), followed
            by sender timestamp and telemetry metadata.

endmenu
